  "subject": "A Peak Tram driver who has tilted the whole of Central sideways for twenty years buys one egg tart a day from the girl at the lower-terminal kiosk and never says more, until on the steepest stretch he presses the wrong button, the announcement mic goes live, and he asks her out in front of two hundred passengers.",
  "caption": "Cantonese 1980s campus folk duo, sunny walking strum. Two steel-string acoustic guitars strumming open chords with fingerpicked answers, soft upright bass, light shaker and brushed snare, a single harmonica phrase between verses. Dry close-miked room recording, warm tape tone, no reverb wash. Male tenor lead, plain and boyish, with a gentle female harmony on the choruses, clearly sung melody on every line. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 100 BPM, G major. Bashful, warm, cheeky. No drums-and-bass pop production, no synths, no autotune, no rap, no electric guitar distortion, no big reverb.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n我揸山頂纜車 揸咗廿年\n成個中環 日日斜喺窗邊\n朝早七點半 山腳嗰個小檔\n有個女仔 賣蛋撻 笑得好甜\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我日日買一個 唔敢講第二句\n佢話 今日仲熱 你快啲食\n\n[Chorus]\n纜車爬上最斜嗰段\n全車人 捉實扶手\n我心跳得 好似個鼓\n點解 就係開唔到口\n\n[Verse]\n成車遊客 舉起部電話\n高樓企得斜 我心都搖晃\n我背熟句子 對住個倒後鏡\n點知手一震 㩒著咗個咪\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n全車即刻靜晒 兩百對耳仔\n我索性 講落去\n\n[Chorus]\n纜車爬上最斜嗰段\n全車人 捉實扶手\n我話蛋撻檔嗰位小姐\n收工之後 同我食餐飯\n\n[Verse]\n一車人拍手 有個阿婆喊\n我望住前面 唔敢回頭\n落到站 佢企喺月台\n手上拎住 兩個蛋撻\n\n[Bridge]\n佢話 我聽到喇\n成個山頂 都聽到喇\n下次你想講 行落嚟講\n\n[Chorus]\n纜車爬上最斜嗰段\n全車人 捉實扶手\n今朝我唔使㩒咪\n佢坐喺我隔籬 食蛋撻\n\n[Outro]\n各位乘客 請捉穩扶手\n前面係最甜嗰一段",
